Set up a vector DB Qdrant using Docker: (Qdrant is an open-source vector database that runs as a Docker container)
step 1: start a Qdrant server
$ docker run -d -p 6333:6333 -p 6334:6334 -v $(pwd)/qdrant_storage:/qdrant/storage:z qdrant/qdrant
    -p 6333:6333     //Exposes the HTTP API and Dashboard
    -p 6334:6334     //Exposes the gRPC API (instead of accepting json or http requests, it accepts binary objects)
    -v $(pwd)/qdrant_storage:/qdrant/storage:z     //mounts the data when the container stops; $(pwd)/qdrant_storage is local storage path; /qdrant/storage is storage path in container
    qdrant/qdrant      //image

verify whether the DB is up on running from terminal:
$ curl -s http://localhost:6333/collections

step 2: Set Up Python and Complete connect_lab.py
navigate to the app directory and Set Up python environment
$ cd ~/app
$ python3 -m venv venv
$ source venv/bin/activate
$ pip install qdrant-client
implement the code and run 
$ python connect_lab.py



